 What are the internal pulls on the STM32F103?
   - D+ (PA12) Pull-Up: The STM32F103 USB peripheral has an internal 1.5kΩ pull-up resistor on D+ (PA12) controlled by the USB peripheral hardware
     (tied to power-down / connect state). Additionally, many STM32F103 boards (like the Blue Pill) have an external physical pull-up resistor on
     PA12 to 3.3V on the PCB.
   - Data Lines (PA11 / PA12): The internal USB transceiver integrates standard receiver termination and weak internal biasing, but does not use
     standard general-purpose GPIO pull-ups/pull-downs. When configured as Input Floating (0x04), the GPIO digital input buffer is disconnected or
     bypassed by the analog USB transceiver, leaving the high-speed differential receiver directly connected to the pins.